      "shortMessage": "Variable 'TempRec' ends with the type-encoding suffix 'Rec'. Name variables after what they represent, not their AL type.",
      "fullMessage": "Hungarian notation encodes the variable's type into its name (e.g. 'LoggerCu', 'CustomerRec', 'ClockIface'). This is redundant because the type is visible in the declaration, and it creates maintenance noise when types change. Name variables after the role they play in the code instead. Note: Label suffixes (Lbl, Msg, Err, Qst, Tok, Cap, Txt) are accepted convention and are not flagged.",
